  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Success without significance - purpose, service, and meaningful relationships - is not really success at all. It's important to properly reflect on how we can live a meaningful life not just with the superficial trappings of \"success\" but with deep purpose and joy in all we do. \n\nAsk yourself:  What is the core purpose of my work and the ways in which it makes the world better? Who are the key relationships in my life, and how can I deepen them? What more can I do at work, at home, and in my community to serve others? How am I becoming better each day? Read [this article](<HBR_Finding_Success_Starts_with_Finding_Your_Purpose>) to learn more.",
